# limit-anchor configuration — copy to anchor.conf to use.
#   cp anchor.conf.example anchor.conf
# anchor-ping.sh sources this file if it exists. Everything is optional.

# Path to the claude CLI. Timers get a minimal PATH, so if `claude` lives in a
# version manager's shim directory, spell it out here.
# CLAUDE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/claude

# Model for the ping. Keep it the cheapest one — this call exists to start a
# clock, not to think.
# CC_ANCHOR_MODEL=haiku

# Hard cap on a single ping, in seconds. Must stay below your timer's own
# start-timeout (the systemd unit installs with TimeoutStartSec=20m).
# CC_ANCHOR_TIMEOUT=900

# Scratch working directory for the ping, kept empty on purpose so the CLI has
# no project context to load.
# CC_ANCHOR_PING_CWD="$HOME/.cache/limit-anchor-ping"

# --- optional integration with a pause-at-threshold guard -------------------
# Off by default: this starter does not ship such a guard, and stamping a file
# nothing reads is just confusing. Turn it on only if you run a PreToolUse hook
# that pauses when a window is nearly spent, and point STATE at its state file.
# CC_ANCHOR_STAMP_GUARD_STATE=1
# CC_LIMIT_GUARD_STATE="$HOME/.claude/rate-limit-state.json"
# CC_LIMIT_GUARD_THRESHOLD=98
# CC_LIMIT_GUARD_STATE_TTL=21600
